  "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+4)x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+4 & =(-x+B)x+({x}^{2}+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)+4 & =(-1+B)(1)+({1}^{2}+4) \\\\ 5 & =-1+B+5 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
